# BuildKit-specific naming (<dockerfile>.dockerignore, co-located with the
# Dockerfile it applies to) — deliberately NOT a root .dockerignore, and
# replaces the old images/trainer/.dockerignore (dead since the context
# move: that file is neither at the context root nor co-located under this
# name, so BuildKit never reads it any more — see MODEL-SERVE-003's context
# move in the Dockerfile itself). The build context for images/trainer/
# Dockerfile is now the repo root (packages/py-scaling lives outside
# images/trainer), so without this every other app, node_modules, .git, and
# every local .venv in the monorepo would enter the build context. This
# file scopes it back down to the two trees the Dockerfile actually COPYs,
# then excludes local-only noise inside those — same discipline the old
# file stated about itself: "load-bearing, not housekeeping."

# Everything else at the repo root — the Dockerfile only ever COPYs
# images/trainer/ and packages/py-scaling/.
*
!images/trainer
!packages/py-scaling
!images/trainer/**
!packages/py-scaling/**

# Stale caches from local dev. Harmless at import (Python 3 will not import
# a .pyc without its .py in __pycache__), but they bloat the image and their
# mtimes break the build-time compileall's timestamp match, causing every
# module to be re-parsed on every run.
images/trainer/**/__pycache__/
images/trainer/*.py[cod]
images/trainer/**/*$py.class
images/trainer/.pytest_cache/
images/trainer/.mypy_cache/
images/trainer/.ruff_cache/

# Tests live outside app/ in this layout, so they are not copied by the
# COPY above — listed anyway so the exclusion survives someone moving them
# in. Both spellings: this image uses test/, but tests/ is the more common
# convention and would otherwise ship silently if the directory were
# renamed.
images/trainer/test/
images/trainer/tests/
images/trainer/conftest.py
images/trainer/.coverage
images/trainer/htmlcov/

# Never, under any circumstance — this container is credential-free by
# design, same statement the old .dockerignore made about itself.
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/credentials*
**/secrets*
images/trainer/.env
images/trainer/.env.*

# Local scratch that has a habit of appearing next to the code.
images/trainer/*.parquet
images/trainer/*.joblib
images/trainer/*.ipynb
images/trainer/.ipynb_checkpoints/
images/trainer/notebooks/
images/trainer/scratch/
images/trainer/tmp/
images/trainer/.impeccable/

packages/py-scaling/**/__pycache__/
packages/py-scaling/.pytest_cache/
packages/py-scaling/tests/
packages/py-scaling/src/*.egg-info/

# The old Dockerfile/.dockerignore themselves — not copied, but excluded
# from the build context hash too.
images/trainer/Dockerfile
images/trainer/Dockerfile.dockerignore
images/trainer/.dockerignore
